# Agent workflow (mandatory)

## Never use the dev server for UI testing or demos

- Do **not** run `npm run dev`, `vite`, or `localhost` URLs to test, verify, or show the UI.
- Do **not** use screen recordings or screenshots taken from a local dev server as walkthrough evidence.
- UI validation and walkthroughs must use the **deployed GitHub Pages app** after changes are on `main`:
  - **https://thisguyse19.github.io/iwant/**
- Pushes to `main` trigger the deploy workflow (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) → `gh-pages`.
- After merging, wait for the deploy workflow to finish, then test on the live site (hard-refresh or reinstall PWA if needed).
- `npm run build` is fine for compile checks only; it is not a substitute for live UI testing.

## Always merge completed work to `main`

- Do **not** leave finished work on an open PR branch without merging.
- When a task is complete and builds pass, **merge to `main`** (squash or merge commit per repo convention).
- Do not treat "PR created" as done — merge is required unless the user explicitly asks to hold the PR open.
